From: Project Arctic
Subject: shell32: the desktop's icons never get an empty work area.

The view of the desktop's icons takes the work area. A shell that started
while the monitors were being made anew (winlogon restarted it after a
display mode change, 2026-11-18) read an empty one, and its icons stayed
in a view of 0x0 until the shell was started again: the wallpaper and the
widgets were there, the icons not. An empty work area is the whole screen.
---
diff --git a/dll/win32/shell32/shelldesktop/CDesktopBrowser.cpp b/dll/win32/shell32/shelldesktop/CDesktopBrowser.cpp
--- a/dll/win32/shell32/shelldesktop/CDesktopBrowser.cpp
+++ b/dll/win32/shell32/shelldesktop/CDesktopBrowser.cpp
@@ -217,9 +217,10 @@
     SetRect(&rcScreen, GetSystemMetrics(SM_XVIRTUALSCREEN), GetSystemMetrics(SM_YVIRTUALSCREEN),
             GetSystemMetrics(SM_XVIRTUALSCREEN) + GetSystemMetrics(SM_CXVIRTUALSCREEN),
             GetSystemMetrics(SM_YVIRTUALSCREEN) + GetSystemMetrics(SM_CYVIRTUALSCREEN));
-    SystemParametersInfoW(SPI_GETWORKAREA, 0, &rcNewSize, 0);
+    if (!SystemParametersInfoW(SPI_GETWORKAREA, 0, &rcNewSize, 0) || IsRectEmpty(&rcNewSize))
+        rcNewSize = rcScreen;
     if (IsRectEmpty(&rcScreen))
         rcScreen = rcNewSize;
     ::MoveWindow(m_hWnd, rcScreen.left, rcScreen.top, rcScreen.right - rcScreen.left, rcScreen.bottom - rcScreen.top, TRUE);
     ::MoveWindow(m_hWndShellView, rcNewSize.left - rcScreen.left, rcNewSize.top - rcScreen.top,
                  rcNewSize.right - rcNewSize.left, rcNewSize.bottom - rcNewSize.top, TRUE);
